"success","api_error_status":null,"result":"**Key closure-risk indicators for a young '40 Act ETF:**\n\n**Seed capital**\n- **Seed vs. AUM:** If seed money is still most of AUM, the fund is fragile.\n- **Seed terms:** Seeders, often market makers, usually exit after 6–12 months. Watch for redemptions then.\n- **Concentration:** If a few holders own most shares, one exit can shrink the fund sharply.\n\n**Sponsor economics**\n- **Breakeven AUM:** Fixed costs (admin, custody, index licensing, listing, audit) often run $250k–$500k+ yearly. Many funds need about $25–50M to cover them.\n- **Fee waivers/caps:** Large or expiring waivers mean the sponsor is subsidizing the fund.\n- **Sponsor health:** Lineup size, past closures, white-label trust use.\n- **Flows and liquidity:** Net creations, spreads, volume.\n- **Distribution:** Platform and model-portfolio placements.\n\nThese are signals, not predictions of closure.","ttft_ms":2514,"type":"result","duration_ms":5029,"uuid":"b8d3030e-b35b-496b-9422-9f1cece2c746","ttft_stream_ms":1261,"time_to_request_ms":72,"first_content_frame_ms":1261,"queued_turn_count":0,"result_index":0,"credential_expires_at":"2026-11-28T06:36:39.484Z"}
